{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Claim money on the claim form (foreign-currency and multi-line claims), the same rules as the web form (apps/web/src/routes/_app/claims/-lib/money.ts) and the server (packages/core/src/claims/money.ts). Amounts are integers in the currency's minor units (ISO 4217 exponent), rates are SGD per 1 unit with at most 6 decimals, held as millionths. A line's SGD amount is roundHalfUp(amountMinor x rateMicros x 100 / (10^exponent x 10^6)), rounded once per line; the claim total is the sum of the rounded lines.",
  "rules": [
    "An amount is positive, has at most 15 whole digits and at most `exponent` decimals (none for exponent 0); commas are ignored. Anything else is invalid (null).",
    "A rate is a positive decimal with 1 to 9 whole digits and at most 6 decimals. Anything else is invalid (null).",
    "An SGD line's SGD amount is its amount. A foreign line has no SGD amount (null) until both its amount and rate are valid.",
    "A result that is not a safe integer (above 9007199254740991) is invalid (null); the server refuses it too.",
    "The receipt rule of a claim type applies to the line's SGD amount: 'always' needs one, 'above' needs one when the SGD amount is more than receiptAboveCents, 'never' doesn't.",
    "The messages are shown under the field once something is typed."
  ],
